package dev.kb896.aiusage.rear

import android.graphics.Path
import androidx.core.graphics.PathParser
import dev.kb896.aiusage.data.PanelTheme

/**
 * The GLASS theme's glyphs: solid shapes, where ORIGINAL's are traced rectangles.
 *
 * GENERATED by tools/glass-icons.py from Material Symbols — do not edit path data by hand.
 *
 * Material Symbols Rounded, filled, Apache 2.0, https://github.com/google/material-design-icons.
 * Rounded and filled for the same reason the theme exists: a solid shape with soft corners
 * sits beside a proportional face the way line work does not, and it matches the panes.
 *
 * Two earlier attempts are worth naming, because both were wrong in ways that only showed
 * on the panel. Hand-drawn glyphs were ten chances to get a proportion slightly off and
 * they were not consistent with one another — the camera came out as a figure eight. Then
 * an outline set, which is coherent but hollow: at twenty units on a dark panel an
 * outlined glyph is a thin ring that disappears, where a filled one holds.
 *
 * THESE ARE SQUARE, and ORIGINAL's traced glyphs are not: its battery is tall and narrow,
 * its camera wide. So the footprint is a property of the THEME rather than of the panel,
 * and everything that lays out against a glyph asks for it through Glyphs.aspect.
 */
object GlassIcons {

    /** One glyph, as Material's own path data on its own grid. */
    class Outline(val data: String) {
        /** Parsed lazily and kept — PathParser is a scan, and this is asked per frame. */
        val path: Path by lazy { PathParser.createPathFromPathData(data) }
    }

    /**
     * The grid these are drawn on, and where its origin sits.
     *
     * Material Symbols use a 960-unit box with the Y axis running from -960 to 0, so a
     * glyph has to be moved down by a full box before it is anywhere near the cell it was
     * asked for. Stated here rather than baked into the path data: the data is generated
     * and should stay exactly as the source has it, so that regenerating it is a copy
     * rather than a transformation somebody has to reproduce.
     */
    const val VIEWPORT = 960.0f
    const val ORIGIN_Y = -960.0f

    /** Square, all of them. */
    const val ASPECT = 1f

